https://stream.mux.com/v69RSHhFelSm4701snP22dYz2jICy4E4FUyk02rW4gxRM.m3u8

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# PER-CHANNEL OPTIONS (#EXTVLCOPT)
# Some servers reject you unless you send the right headers. These lines
# go BETWEEN the #EXTINF and the URL. VLC and most IPTV apps honour them;
# a browser cannot set them, which is one reason native wrappers matter.
#
#   #EXTINF:-1 group-title="Example",Picky Server
#   #EXTVLCOPT:http-user-agent=Mozilla/5.0
#   #EXTVLCOPT:http-referrer=https://example.com/
#   http://example.com/stream.m3u8
#
# GROUPING, THE OLD WAY
# Before group-title existed, players used a separate directive. You may
# still meet it in the wild, so a good parser handles both. The app
# supports this too:
#
#   #EXTGRP:Sports
#
# COMMENTS
# Any line starting with # that is not a known directive is ignored, which
# is how this whole tutorial sits inside a valid playlist file. Try loading
# this very file in your app via the File tab — it will work.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
